## Phase 12 — DuckDB Time-Series Store + Historical Replay
*Depends on Phase 9. ~3 days.*

Implements REQ-5: DVR-style replay.

#### [NEW] `src/storage/duckdb_store.py`
Persistent columnar store using DuckDB. Schema:
```sql
-- Constraint snapshots (one row per constraint per interval)
CREATE TABLE constraint_intervals (
    interval         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    constraint_name  VARCHAR NOT NULL,
    canonical_id     VARCHAR,
    shadow_price     DOUBLE,
    limit_mw         DOUBLE,
    monitored_mw     DOUBLE,
    pct_of_limit     DOUBLE,
    state            VARCHAR,
    PRIMARY KEY (interval, constraint_name)
);

-- Shift factor snapshots (stored per solve, not per interval)
CREATE TABLE shift_factor_snapshots (
    solved_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    node         VARCHAR NOT NULL,
    constraint   VARCHAR NOT NULL,
    shift_factor DOUBLE,
    r2_score     DOUBLE,
    n_intervals  INTEGER
);

-- LMP snapshots (MCC component only)
CREATE TABLE lmp_intervals (
    interval             TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    settlement_location  VARCHAR NOT NULL,
    mcc                  DOUBLE,
    PRIMARY KEY (interval, settlement_location)
);
```

Partitioned by date for fast range queries. DuckDB handles this via date-range predicates on `interval` with Parquet files under `src/data/timeseries/`.

