### REQ-1: The "What-If" Sensitivity Matrix

> *"I need your engine to calculate the delta of the MCC before it clears."*
>
> `MCC_Node = -Σ (SF_Node,c × ShadowPrice_c)`

**Status:** 🟡 Partially built — the math exists, real-time delivery does not.

| Sub-Feature | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Shift factor calculation (SF × SP per node) | ✅ Built | `ShiftFactorCalculator` — but offline/batch only |
| **Shift Factor Exposure column** (GSF × SP) | ❌ Not built | Simple multiplication, needs output format added |
| **Real-time MCC prediction** (pre-clearing) | ❌ Not built | Requires live shadow price feed + cached SFs |
| **Dynamic Flow Impact Calculator** | ❌ Not built | "Inject 50MW at Node A → how much flows on Line X?" — this is a PTDF bilateral query |

#### Engineering Notes
- **Exposure column** is trivial: add `sf_exposure = shift_factor × shadow_price` to output DataFrame and the API response. Already have all the inputs.
- **Pre-clearing MCC prediction** requires subscribing to SPP's RTBM price feed (published every 5 minutes at `portal.spp.org`) and applying cached SFs. Latency target: compute in <500ms after each new RTBM publish.
- **Dynamic Flow Impact**: for a bilateral injection (source node A, sink node B), the line flow change on constraint c is: `ΔFlow_c = (SF_A,c - SF_B,c) × ΔMW`. Our solver already produces SF_A,c and SF_B,c — just need a query endpoint.

