### REQ-4: Millisecond APIs & Data Ingestion Pipeline

> *"Sub-minute ingestion. API-first. Raw JSON streams."*

**Status:** ❌ Not built — architecture design required

| Sub-Feature | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| SPP RTBM scraper (5-min batch) | ✅ Built | `RTConstraintsScraper` + `RTBMLMPScraper` |
| **Sub-60s streaming ingestion loop** | ❌ Not built | Need a daemon process + SPP portal polling |
| **REST API for shift factors** | ❌ Not built | FastAPI or Flask — `GET /shift-factors?node=X&constraint=Y` |
| **WebSocket / SSE push for live data** | ❌ Not built | Push new constraint state to connected dashboards |
| **JSON stream for algo ingestion** | ❌ Not built | `GET /stream/constraints` → newline-delimited JSON |

#### Architecture Recommendation
```
SPP Portal (every 5 min)
    └─→ Ingest Worker (asyncio polling daemon)
         ├─→ Constraint Normalizer + Registry
         ├─→ Regime Detector
         ├─→ Shift Factor Cache (Redis or in-memory dict)
         └─→ FastAPI server
              ├─→ REST: GET /api/v1/shift-factors
              ├─→ REST: GET /api/v1/constraints/live
              ├─→ REST: GET /api/v1/mcc?node=X
              ├─→ REST: POST /api/v1/flow-impact  (bilateral what-if)
              ├─→ WebSocket: /ws/constraints  (push updates)
              └─→ REST: GET /api/v1/portfolio/risk  (after position upload)
```

SPP RTBM updates every **5 minutes** — true sub-minute ingestion is only possible with private ISO real-time telemetry feeds (ICCP/SCADA), which are not publicly available for SPP. Realistic target for public data: **<30s latency from SPP publish to our API response**.

