### REQ-5: Historical Replay & Backtesting ("DVR Mode")

> *"Select a date/time, replay interval-by-interval, compare predicted vs. actual shadow prices."*

**Status:** ❌ Not built — needs time-series storage + replay API

| Sub-Feature | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Historical constraint + LMP data | 🟡 Partial | Scrapers work but no persistent time-series store |
| **Interval-by-interval replay API** | ❌ Not built | `GET /replay?date=2024-11-01&interval=02:55` |
| **Predicted vs. actual shadow price comparison** | ❌ Not built | Requires a shadow price forecasting model (ML) |
| **Shift factor evolution over time** | ❌ Not built | Need to snapshot SF matrix per interval and store it |
| **P&L attribution by interval** | ❌ Not built | Apply position MW × SF × ΔSP across replay window |

#### Engineering Notes
- **Storage:** A time-series DB is ideal (TimescaleDB, InfluxDB, or DuckDB columnar). Minimum viable: DuckDB parquet files partitioned by date.
- **Shadow price forecasting** for "predicted vs. actual" is a significant ML scope — at minimum, a regime-based persistence model (assume next interval = current interval's shadow prices) + a more sophisticated LSTM/gradient boosting model trained on historical intervals.
- This is the highest-complexity feature. Recommend building the data storage layer first (so historical data accumulates), then the replay API, then the forecasting model.

